{#- One sign per day of the week's lunch specials, for the board on the
    wall (client 2026-10-10: read from 6 to 14 feet). Shared by
    sign-day-specials.njk (colour) and sign-day-specials-bw.njk (`bw: true`).

    Each day is its own letter-landscape page, so the PDF prints the week
    as a stack and any one day can be printed again on its own (print page
    3 for Wednesday). The week is the newest one in specials.json, like the
    weekly post and the counter sign.

    SIZED FOR DISTANCE. About an inch of letter height reads at ten feet,
    so the plate is set at 1.2in (letters about 0.85in tall) and nothing on
    the sheet is under 0.3in. That is why the sign says "Choice of
    side" and doesn't list the salads: at a size that fits, nobody past the
    counter could read them. The soup is a separate item, so it has its own
    box at the foot of the sheet, with its price. -#}
{%- set week = specials.days | latestWeek %}
{%- set soupCat = (menu.categories | where("id", "soup"))[0] %}
<div class="ds-stack">
    {%- for d in week %}
    {#- Bare ("Choice of side", "A, B"): "with" costs a line at this size. -#}
    {%- set sides = d | specialSides(true) %}
    <div class="canvas sign ds{% if bw %} sign--bw{% endif %}">
        <header class="ds-top">
            <p class="p-display ds-day ink-accent">{{ d.date | dayDate("weekday") }}</p>
            <p class="ds-date ink-teal">{{ d.date | dayDate("monthDay") }}</p>
            <p class="p-label ds-when ink-teal">From 11am</p>
        </header>

        <div class="ds-main">
            {#- A name longer than any so far steps down a size, so it still
                fits in two lines. -#}
            <p class="p-display ds-special{% if d.special.length > 24 %} ds-special--long{% endif %} ink-teal">{{ d.special }}</p>
            {%- if sides %}
            <p class="ds-sides">{{ sides }}</p>
            {%- endif %}
            {%- if specials.includesDrink %}
            <p class="ds-drink ink-accent">Includes a drink</p>
            {%- endif %}
        </div>

        {%- if d.soup %}
        <footer class="ds-soup">
            <div class="ds-soup-head">
                <p class="p-label ds-soup-label ink-accent">Soup of the day</p>
                {%- if soupCat and soupCat.items %}
                <p class="ds-soup-price">{% for s in soupCat.items %}{% if not loop.first %} &middot; {% endif %}{{ s.name }} {{ s.price | money }}{% endfor %}</p>
                {%- endif %}
            </div>
            <p class="p-display ds-soup-name ink-teal">{{ d.soup }}</p>
        </footer>
        {%- endif %}
    </div>
    {%- endfor %}
</div>
